Step 2: Address the condition-dependence argument. While it is scientifically accurate that argon can become conductive when ionized into a plasma under high-energy conditions, scientific questions regarding elemental properties assume standard temperature and pressure (STP) unless specific conditions are explicitly stated. At STP, neutral argon is an electrical insulator with resistivity orders of magnitude higher than that of any metal. To define an element by its behavior under extreme, non-standard conditions would make the category of "elemental conductivity" meaningless compared to fixed metallic standards.

